# Code owners for this repository.
#
# REPLACE @YOUR_GITHUB_USER with your GitHub username or team (a team is written
# @org/team-name). Until you do, GitHub's Settings > Code owners page reports
# every line as an unknown owner and no reviewer is ever requested — the file is
# inert rather than wrong, but it buys you nothing.
#
# Owners are auto-requested as reviewers when a PR touches their paths. Nothing
# here blocks a merge until you turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in
# branch protection, so treat these as routing until a second person has write
# access.
#
# Last match wins, so the specific entries below override the default.

# Default owner for anything not matched more specifically.
*                           @YOUR_GITHUB_USER

# --- Application layers -----------------------------------------------------
# The dependency direction is enforced at build time by the layer map in
# Directory.Build.props; these entries are about who reviews a change to each
# layer, not about what may reference what.
/Template.Common/           @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.ServiceDefaults/  @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.Business/         @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.Data/             @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.Client/           @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.Worker/           @YOUR_GITHUB_USER

# Aspire orchestration: a change here alters how every service is wired and run.
/Template.AppHost/          @YOUR_GITHUB_USER

# --- Build, CI, and quality gates ------------------------------------------
# Workflows hold the deploy path and the release process; the layer map and the
# coverage floors are what keep the architecture and the test suite honest.
/.github/                   @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Directory.Build.props      @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Directory.Build.targets    @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Directory.Packages.props   @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/coverage.runsettings       @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/eng/                       @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/global.json                @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/Template.slnx              @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/.editorconfig              @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
/.dockerignore              @YOUR_GITHUB_USER

# --- Architecture decisions -------------------------------------------------
# An ADR is the record of why something is the way it is. Reversing one is a
# deliberate act, not a drive-by edit.
/docs/adr/                  @YOUR_GITHUB_USER
